+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-reject-impossible-instants/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+## Context
+
+`parseInstant` checks a regex shape and `Date.parse`, which rolls some impossible values over.
+
+## Decisions
+
+After parsing, compare the first 19 characters (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`) of `new Date(ms).toISOString()` with those of the input; throw if they differ. Fractional seconds are ignored in the comparison, so they stay accepted as before.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-reject-impossible-instants/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-reject-impossible-instants/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a25e2cfdbb4de8e287788c11730816323698ed2d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-reject-impossible-instants/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+## Why
+
+`parseInstant` accepts impossible calendar dates (`2026-02-30T00:00:00Z`) and `T24:00:00Z`, silently rolling them over to another date. `quote`, `book`, `availability` and `cancel` then reserve or refund on a date other than the one given.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Reject timestamps whose date-time does not survive a round trip through the parsed instant, so impossible dates and 24:00 are errors.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+(none)
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: timestamps that name a non-existent date or time are invalid.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/period.ts` (`parseInstant`) and its tests.
